1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The most popular satirical poems of the time were on Tverskoy Boulevard; Here are examples of this tabloid wit:
2 CONT
2 CONT I'm sorry to part with the boulevard!
2 CONT You don't want to go there...
2 CONT There you look at the dear ones for nothing
2 CONT And you tear joy for nothing.
2 CONT Everywhere the group is beautiful
2 CONT Appear to the eyes
2 CONT How dangerous are their arrows?
2 CONT And how harmful to the hearts.
2 CONT There in a green corset
2 CONT Silently Durova walks
2 CONT Her in a plush vest
2 CONT The brother leads by the hand.
2 CONT Both sigh softly
2 CONT And the boulevard is no longer nice to them,
2 CONT They suffer from love
2 CONT The whole world is disgusted for them ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is '''Anyuta Trubetskaya'''
2 CONT Running headlong,
2 CONT Nodding at everything
2 CONT Gives everyone smiles.
2 CONT Behind her is the venerable grandfather
2 CONT Following in her footsteps
2 CONT Peace of the precious granddaughter
2 CONT Protects the eyes better.
2 CONT Is the breeze blowing softly
2 CONT He will cover with a handkerchief,
2 CONT Or is the sun hotter
2 CONT It will protect you from the heat.
2 CONT
2 CONT Trubetskoy, Prince Sergei Nikolaevich, retired lieutenant general, lived on Pokrovka; the house of the prince was called “chest of drawers” due to the strange architecture, and in the house and the whole Trubetskoy family - Trubet
2 CONC skoy “Chest of drawers”.
2 CONT
2 CONT And behind them an adjutant
2 CONT Prince Golitsyn is running there.
2 CONT With his chamberlain's bow
2 CONT Makes us all laugh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here Bolkhovskaya flies,
2 CONT Curving the right side
2 CONT Crooked, oblique,
2 CONT Like vomit powder.
2 CONT Yes, and little sister
2 CONT Will not give in to her in anything,
2 CONT Lonely feathered bird
2 CONT You can rejoice in...
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is Popovich Malinovsky
2 CONT He also performs here.
2 CONT Behind him plump Watkowski,
2 CONT At what weight is thirty pounds.
2 CONT He leads his wife by the arm
2 CONT As thick as it is
2 CONT Like a laugh, everyone is fat in a bunch
2 CONT Gathered together.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is Maikov, a music lover,
2 CONT Reciting goes.
2 CONT As a theater manager
2 CONT He leads all the actors.
2 CONT Mochalov, Zubov, Kolpakov
2 CONT He is escorted with respect,
2 CONT Lisitsyn, Zlov and Kandakov
2 CONT They clear the way for him.
2 CONT All authors strive for it,
2 CONT Tragedy is in their hands.
2 CONT They all choke, crowd,
2 CONT Bring the gift of their minds
2 CONT Take it, take it, they proclaim
2 CONT Oh, Maikov, you are these works!
2 CONT With these words they throw
2 CONT It has its own tragedy.
2 CONT
2 CONT And Volkonsky from the carousel
2 CONT Rolled in sonorous spurs,
2 CONT All disheveled, as from a bed,
2 CONT This guy is really nice.
2 CONT
2 CONT An unknown piit ends his poem "To the boulevards" with the following words:
2 CONT
2 CONT But not everyone, after all, to the crumbs
2 CONT We write here
2 CONT Isn't it time to take a droshky
2 CONT Yes, go home to sleep. 
