1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Russian Nobleman Migrated to UK and worked privately. Gained a reputation for larceny and bribery in London and appeared in 1911 in The Old Bailey in which he pleaded his noble rank to make sure he was set free but
2 CONC  they deemed that irrelevant regarding the crime. In 1912 he was put in a lunacy asylum.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most likely he had little connection with his close family although managed to  make a wealthy living before being arrested for numerous crimes in London, Brussels and Paris. It is strange that his role as a Prince may have been m
2 CONC otivation for him thinking he could get away with it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Allegedly in 1930 he died in Finland of Lung Cancer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Used alias last name Makieff in Belgium and France when arrested although used naturlised name in 1911 UK census.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possibly changed name or uses various alias
