1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT '''Solomon Hammond''' was born on March 14, 1815 in Russell County, Virginia, United States. His parents were [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664371945 Robert Hammond] and [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664372217 Rachel (Colley) 
2 CONC Hammond]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664371939 Amanda (Belcher) Hammond] on March 6, 1842 in Lawrence County, Ohio, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664371947 Robe
2 CONC rt Hammond]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664372734 Margaret A. (...) Hammond] on September 23, 1845 in Lawrence County, Kentucky, United States. Together they had the following children: [https://www.geni.com/profile-346643
2 CONC 91352 Hiram Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664391358 Amanda Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664391365 Jane Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664391469 Richard Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34
2 CONC 664391376 Elizabeth Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664391386 Solomon Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664391393 Rachael Ann Hammond]; [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664391412 Charles Hammond]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon married [https://www.geni.com/profile-34664372792 Amanda (Dyer) Hammond] on March 29, 1863 in Lawrence County, Ohio, United States. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on September 8, 1894 in Lawrence County, Ohio, United States. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Solomon was a son of Robert Hammond and Rachel Colley. His brother Richard Hammond married 1847 Nancy Robison in Lawrence County, Ohio. Solomon and his wife Amanda Belcher had a son Robert Hammond born 24 April 1843 in Ohio. That 
2 CONC Robert would be an attractive candidate for the Robert who was raised by Rufus and Elizabeth Roberson because he was an only child, his mother died when he was five months old, and his father did not remarry until 1845. However, t
2 CONC hat Robert, age 17, appears on the 1860 census at Perry, Lawrence County, Ohio in the household of his father Solomon.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': 1880 - Perry, Lawrence, Ohio, United States
2 CONT
