1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Constantine Iosifovich Trishatny (Russian: Константин Иосифович Тришатный) continued the military traditions of his anchestors and entered the 2nd "Konstantinovskoe" Military School (Russian: 2-е военное Константин
2 CONC овское училище). In service from September, 12 [O.S. August, 31] 1887 what indirectly shows he was born about 1869–70. On its graduation on August, 21 [O.S. 9] 1888 was promoted to the rank of podporuchik and seconded to the 74th 
2 CONC "Stavropol" regiment. On August, 22 [O.S. 10] 1889 seconded to the guards unit maintaining the rank of podporuchik (lieutenant). Promoted to poruchik on August, 22 [O.S. 10] 1893, to stabskapitän (May, 18 [O.S. 6] 1900); to captai
2 CONC n (May, 18 [O.S. 6] 1900); to colonel (December, 18 [O.S. 6] 1910). As of March 1914 registered with 1st Leib Guard Rifle regiment.
2 CONT
2 CONT In World War I, on April, 9 [O.S. March, 27] 1915 he assumed command of 54th ("Minsk") Rifle regiment; on January, 22 [O.S. 9] 1916 of a brigade of 37th Infantry division with a promotion to Major General (1916). On October, 23 [O
2 CONC .S. 10] 1916 assumed command of the 41st Infantry division. In September 1918 was taken as a hostage by the North-Caucasian Soviet Republic in the provision of a truce. After the violation of the armistice, following the coup of I
2 CONC . L. Sorokin executed in Pyatigorsk together with the other hostages. Awards: Order of Saint Stanislaus 2nd grade (1909); Order of St. Anna 2nd grade (1912).[12]
2 CONT
