2 CONT Born on October 5, 1858 in Moscow. On October 21 of the same year in Nikola Church in Nikola Church, the suspension was his grandfather - Peter-General Prince Peter Ivanovich Trubetsky (1798-1871), Akhtydka estate owner and aunt -
2 CONC  County SV Tolstaya Student, whose PN Trubetsky was with his Sisters Sofia and Maria after death mother. As a child, they went into real estate narrow. Their father, Director of the Moscow branch of the Imperial Russian Music Soci
2 CONC ety (RMO) Prince Nikolai Petrovich Trubetsky was married again in 1861 - Sofia Alexeyevna Lopukhina (1841-1901), from the second marriage NP Trubetsky had ten children - a summary of the brothers and sisters P. N. Trubetsky; The m
2 CONC ost prominent among them were the famous university professors and philosophers Sergei and Yevgeny Nikolayevich Trubetsky.
2 CONT
2 CONT After graduating from the Faculty of Law of Moscow University, P. N. Trubetsky started serving in the department of the Ministry of Internal Affairs. In 1883, he first "held the position" of the Moscow district leader of the nobil
2 CONC ity, replacing the schedule of A. V. Bobrinsky, then from him S. V. Tolstoy moved to real estate near Moscow (officially sold a sufficiently small amount of such ownership). In 1884, the aade replaced the provincial governor. Then
2 CONC  the posts of county and provincial leaders P. N. Trubetsky received the election.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a wedding on October 1, 1884 with Princess Alexandra Vladimirovna Obolenskaja (1861-1939), they left for a trip to Europe.
2 CONT
2 CONT The head of the Moscow province of the nobility P. N. Trubetsky was from 1892 to 1906. In parallel, he became a member of the Court of Justice and civil and civil laundry, taking the road from Junker to Egmerster and in 1896 becam
2 CONC e a real statistical adviser.
2 CONT
2 CONT P. N. Trubetsky belonged to a number of things in the southern regions of the country: p. Kozatack Kherson Province, DolMatovo Tavrichesky Province, Sochi (Arduche) Black Sea Province. Major winemaker, he was one of the founders (
2 CONC 1901) of the Committee of Viticulture and Wine Making of the Imperial Moscow Agricultural Society. In Kozatskis, except for numerous vineyards in 1896, there was a good sheep "- one of the best in Russia and a large riding company
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 31, 1900 in the narrow, where Sergei Nikolayevich Trubetsky lived, Office P. N. Trubetsky, the famous philosopher Vladimir Sergeevich Solovyov died. P. N. Trubetsky attended the funeral at NovoDevichy Monastery.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the spring of 1905, PN Trubetsky with Prince AG Shcherbatov, Graphs Pavlom and Peter Dmitriptichi Sheremetev, publishers NA Pavlov and SF Sharapov and others became the founder and main employee of the monarchical union of the 
2 CONC Russian people in Moscow (after winning the First State Duma elections the union's activities declined sharply; many of its members became participants in other black-monarchical organizations).
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1906, he was elected a noble of the societies to the Council of State (PN Trubetsky and the number of the mayor of St. Petersburg with VV Guddovich, supported by Minister of the Interior PN RUNOVOVO, as part of a separate repre
2 CONC sentation in the Council of State. The Council was later headed by the Land Commission. The famous liberalism is seen as the chairman of the groups, and the parties received, as a rule, only persons who fell into the upper house o
2 CONC f the Russian parliament into account for the election and the appointment of Nicholas II. 
2 CONT
