1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In 1859 they settled on a wilderness tract of 146 acres on Breeding
2 CONT
2 CONT Frying Pan, a gift from Mary's father. He was a farmer and a teacher;
2 CONT
2 CONT served in Co E 21st Va Cav, 1863-65, belonged to Sulphur Spring
2 CONT
2 CONT Primitive Baptist Church; served two years as justice of the peace,
2 CONT
2 CONT Buchannan Co., was elected and served as the first Treasurer of
2 CONT
2 CONT Dickenson Co. Both buried on homeplace.
2 CONT
2 CONT - Some Descendants of John Counts of Glade Hollow
2 CONT
2 CONT REFN: 5-24
2 CONT
2 CONT See "Some Descendants of John Counts of Glade Hollow (SoutwestVirginia) 1772-1977" by Elihu Jasper Southerland and Hetty SwindallSutherland
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first Treasurer of Dickenson County, Va when it was createdfrom Russell County. His picture was hung in the Treasurers Office,April 23, 1993. Some newspaper descriptions of the event are in MargeMayfield's possesion. We
2 CONC  attended the ceremony. He served during theCivil War 1863-65 Company E, the 21st Virginia Cavalry.
